[5.210176, "o", "--- SECURITY_REPORT.md ---\r\n"]
[5.21139, "o", "# Security report: cross-organisation file download\r\n\r\nReceived 2026-10-21 through the vulnerability disclosure inbox. Reporter: an independent researcher testing our\r\nstaging stack with the development data. Severity claimed: high.\r\n\r\n## Summary\r\nA logged-in member of one organisation can download a file that belongs to a different organisation by changing the\r\nfile id in the download URL.\r\n\r\n## Steps to reproduce (development database `data/docshare.db`)\r\n1. Log in as Ben Carver, a member of Halden & Price LLP (token in `docs/DEV_USERS.md`).\r\n2. `GET /api/files` lists only Halden & Price LLP files, as expected.\r\n3. Request a file of Marlow Community Clinic, an organisation Ben does not belong to:\r\n   ```\r\n   curl -s -H \"Authorization: Bearer dsk_2e09e4b8245edebc817af708207473b7\" \\\r\n     http://127.0.0.1:8080/api/files/20b5d1d4-8637-49fb-adad-7770457f9573/download\r\n   ```\r\n4. The response is `200` with the full contents of `procurement-request-af6a.txt`.\r\n\r\n## Expected\r\nThe request is refused and no data of "]
[5.211462, "o", "the other organisation is returned.\r\n\r\n## Notes from triage\r\nReproduced on 2026-10-22. File ids are random UUIDs, but they appear in exports, logs and support tickets, so\r\nthey cannot be treated as secret.\r\n"]
[5.211553, "o", "--- PERMISSIONS.md ---\r\n"]
[5.212527, "o", "# docshare access policy\r\n\r\nOwner: platform security. This is the policy every docshare endpoint must follow. Endpoint details are in `API.md`.\r\n\r\n## 1. Who is asking\r\n- Every `/api/...` request must carry `Authorization: Bearer <token>` (the token is `users.token`). A request with no\r\n  token or an unknown token gets `401`. Two endpoints need no login: `GET /api/health` and share links `GET /s/<token>`.\r\n- A user belongs to one or more organisations (rows in `memberships`) and has one role in each: `member` or\r\n  `org_admin`.\r\n- Support staff are users with `users.is_support = 1`. They belong to no organisation and have no home organisation.\r\n\r\n## 2. The active organisation\r\n- Every request acts in one organisation, the *active organisation*: the organisation named in the `X-Org-Id` header,\r\n  or, when the header is absent, the user's home organisation (`users.home_org_id`).\r\n- A member or org_admin may only make active an organisation they belong to. If `X-Org-Id` names any other\r\n  organisation, or one tha"]
[5.212596, "o", "t does not exist, the whole request is refused.\r\n- The caller's role is their role in the active organisation. Someone who is `member` in one organisation and\r\n  `org_admin` in another is an org_admin only while that second organisation is active.\r\n- Members and org_admins act only on folders and files of the active organisation. A file or folder of another\r\n  organisation is refused, even if the caller also belongs to that organisation: they switch first by sending that\r\n  organisation's id in `X-Org-Id`.\r\n- Support may name any existing organisation in `X-Org-Id`; no membership is needed. For support this only chooses\r\n  what the list endpoints show. If support names an organisation that does not exist, the whole request is refused.\r\n  Without `X-Org-Id`, support's list endpoints answer `400`.\r\n\r\n## 3. What each role may do\r\n| Action | Endpoints | member | org_admin | support |\r\n|---|---|---|---|---|\r\n| read | `GET /api/files/<id>` | yes | yes | yes, any organisation |\r\n| download | `GET /api/files/<id>/dow"]
[5.212649, "o", "nload` | yes | yes | yes, any organisation |\r\n| thumb | `GET /api/files/<id>/thumb` | yes | yes | yes, any organisation |\r\n| list | `GET /api/files`, `GET /api/folders`, `GET /api/folders/<id>/files` | yes | yes | yes, the organisation it names |\r\n| export | `POST /api/export` | yes | yes | yes, any organisation |\r\n| rename | `PATCH /api/files/<id>` | yes | yes | no |\r\n| share | `POST /api/files/<id>/shares`, `DELETE /api/shares/<token>` | yes | yes | no |\r\n| delete | `DELETE /api/files/<id>` | no | yes | no |\r\n| support console | `GET /api/admin/orgs` | no | no | yes |\r\n| who am I | `GET /api/me` | yes | yes | yes |\r\n\r\n- For member and org_admin, \"yes\" means: on files and folders of the active organisation only (section 2).\r\n- For support, \"any organisation\" means: any file of any organisation, whatever the active organisation is.\r\n- A list shows exactly the folders or files of the active organisation, and nothing of any other organisation.\r\n\r\n## 4. Export\r\n`POST /api/export` returns several files in one res"]
[5.212686, "o", "ponse. It is allowed only if the caller may `read` every requested\r\nid under the rules above. If even one id is not readable (a file of another organisation, a deleted file, an unknown\r\nid), the whole request is refused and the response holds no file at all.\r\n\r\n## 5. Share links\r\n- Creating a link (`POST /api/files/<id>/shares`) and revoking it (`DELETE /api/shares/<token>`) are the `share`\r\n  action on the link's file.\r\n- Anyone who has the link can download the file with `GET /s/<token>`, without logging in, until the link is revoked\r\n  or the file is deleted. After that, or for an unknown token, the link answers `404`.\r\n\r\n## 6. Refusals\r\n- A refused request gets `403` or `404`; either is fine (404 avoids confirming that an id exists). The only other\r\n  refusal codes are `401` (section 1) and `400` (support listing without `X-Org-Id`, section 2).\r\n- A refusal holds no file data: no file contents and no name of a file the caller may not read. An error message may\r\n  repeat the id it was sent.\r\n- A refused re"]
[5.212729, "o", "quest changes nothing: no file is renamed or deleted, no link is created or revoked.\r\n--- API.md ---\r\n"]
[5.213641, "o", "# docshare API\r\n\r\ndocshare serves the documents that the ingest worker stores in its SQLite database (uploads go through the ingest\r\nworker, not this API). Who may call what is in `PERMISSIONS.md`.\r\n\r\n## Running it\r\n```\r\npython -m docshare.serve --db <path to the SQLite file> --port <port>\r\n```\r\nThe service listens on 127.0.0.1, uses the database file given by `--db` (it must exist; the service never creates\r\none) and keeps all its state there. `python -m docshare.seed --out <path>` builds a fresh development database.\r\n\r\n## Conventions\r\n- Logged-in requests send `Authorization: Bearer <token>`; `X-Org-Id: <organisation id>` chooses the active\r\n  organisation (`PERMISSIONS.md` section 2).\r\n- Request and response bodies are JSON unless stated. Errors are JSON `{\"error\": \"<code>\"}`.\r\n- Ids are UUID strings. Times are ISO 8601 strings in UTC, for example `2026-09-14T10:22:05Z`.\r\n\r\n## Objects\r\n**File**: `id`, `org_id`, `folder_id`, `name`, `mime_type`, `size` (bytes, integer), `uploaded_by` (user id),\r\n`created_a"]
[5.213685, "o", "t`.\r\n\r\n**Folder**: `id`, `org_id`, `name`.\r\n\r\n## Endpoints\r\n| Method and path | Success | Body of a successful response |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| `GET /api/health` | 200 | `{\"ok\": true}`; no login |\r\n| `GET /api/me` | 200 | `{\"user\": {\"id\", \"email\", \"name\", \"is_support\"}, \"active_org_id\", \"role\", \"memberships\": [{\"org_id\", \"role\"}]}`; `active_org_id` is `null` and `role` is `\"support\"` for support without `X-Org-Id` |\r\n| `GET /api/files` | 200 | `{\"files\": [File, ...]}`: the files of the active organisation, sorted by name |\r\n| `GET /api/folders` | 200 | `{\"folders\": [Folder, ...]}`: the folders of the active organisation, sorted by name |\r\n| `GET /api/folders/<folder_id>/files` | 200 | `{\"folder\": Folder, \"files\": [File, ...]}`, files sorted by name |\r\n| `GET /api/files/<file_id>` | 200 | File |\r\n| `GET /api/files/<file_id>/download` | 200 | the file's bytes, with its `mime_type` as Content-Type and `Content-Disposition: attachment; filename=\"<name>\"` |\r\n| `GET /api/files/<file_id>/thumb` | 200 | an `image/svg+xml"]
[5.213738, "o", "` preview: the file name and the first lines of a text file |\r\n| `PATCH /api/files/<file_id>` with `{\"name\": \"<new name>\"}` | 200 | the updated File; the name must be 1 to 200 characters without `/`, else `400` |\r\n| `DELETE /api/files/<file_id>` | 204 | empty; the file and its share links are removed |\r\n| `POST /api/files/<file_id>/shares` | 201 | `{\"token\", \"url\", \"file_id\", \"created_at\"}`; `url` is `/s/<token>` |\r\n| `DELETE /api/shares/<token>` | 204 | empty; the link stops working |\r\n| `GET /s/<token>` | 200 | the file's bytes, like download; no login |\r\n| `POST /api/export` with `{\"file_ids\": [<id>, ...]}` (1 to 50 ids) | 200 | `{\"files\": [{\"id\", \"name\", \"mime_type\", \"size\", \"content_b64\"}, ...]}` in request order; `content_b64` is the file's bytes in standard base64 |\r\n| `GET /api/admin/orgs` | 200 | `{\"orgs\": [{\"id\", \"name\", \"file_count\"}, ...]}` sorted by name |\r\n\r\nMalformed bodies (for example a missing `name`, or `file_ids` that is not a list of 1 to 50 strings) get `400`.\r\n\r\n## Database\r\nThe schema "]
[5.213798, "o", "is in `docshare/db.py` (`SCHEMA`). Tables: `orgs`, `users`, `memberships`, `folders`, `files` (contents\r\nare stored in `files.content`), `shares` (`revoked_at` is set when a link is revoked).\r\n"]
[5.213838, "o", "--- DEV_USERS.md ---\r\n"]
[5.214777, "o", "# Development users\r\n\r\nUsers in the development database `data/docshare.db` (built by `python -m docshare.seed`). The tokens\r\nare development fixtures only.\r\n\r\n| Name | Email | Home organisation | Memberships | Support | Token |\r\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\r\n| Anna Lindqvist | anna@haldenprice.example | Halden & Price LLP | Halden & Price LLP (org_admin) | no | `dsk_c35d7d3b92e4016e27e47ffc284a2d4f` |\r\n| Ben Carver | ben@haldenprice.example | Halden & Price LLP | Halden & Price LLP (member) | no | `dsk_2e09e4b8245edebc817af708207473b7` |\r\n| Chloe Ndiaye | chloe@marlowclinic.example | Marlow Community Clinic | Marlow Community Clinic (org_admin) | no | `dsk_91d5d9efb044d527dd1775a93cdba284` |\r\n| Dev Patel | dev@marlowclinic.example | Marlow Community Clinic | Marlow Community Clinic (member) | no | `dsk_46371f37e9a462ce0fa030a07210d3db` |\r\n| Elena Rossi | elena@tessaract.example | Tessaract Robotics | Tessaract Robotics (org_admin) | no | `dsk_ac0e36d556132dfb84492cd42b1141d6` |\r\n| Felix Brandt | felix@tessaract"]
[5.214835, "o", ".example | Tessaract Robotics | Tessaract Robotics (member) | no | `dsk_c958a7924e9a430cbcfdc56a522162b3` |\r\n| Grace Okafor | grace@okafor-consulting.example | Marlow Community Clinic | Marlow Community Clinic (member), Tessaract Robotics (org_admin) | no | `dsk_1428dfad70ce79934498d7d67c213c12` |\r\n| Riley Chen | riley@support.docshare.example | none | none | yes | `dsk_f9c215672ac38adf41b079157a6d7ff3` |\r\n\r\n| Organisation | Id |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| Halden & Price LLP | `21bade02-6a6a-4768-b2ed-66ffdcc99396` |\r\n| Marlow Community Clinic | `6102dd70-63e8-440e-9dd8-904f07489671` |\r\n| Tessaract Robotics | `83faac57-2f56-4652-866d-e486522c4f8d` |\r\n"]
[5.214932, "o", "--- README.md ---\r\n"]
[5.215913, "o", "# docshare\r\n\r\nThe document sharing API in front of the ingest worker's store: organisations, folders, files, share links and a\r\nsupport console. Python 3.12, Flask, waitress, SQLite.\r\n\r\n- Run: `python -m docshare.serve --db data/docshare.db --port 8080` (from /app).\r\n- Fresh development database: `python -m docshare.seed --out data/docshare.db --force`.\r\n- Feature tests: `python -m pytest -q tests`.\r\n- Docs: `docs/API.md` (endpoints), `docs/PERMISSIONS.md` (who may do what), `docs/DEV_USERS.md` (development users\r\n  and tokens).\r\n- Open security report: `SECURITY_REPORT.md`.\r\n\r\nLayout: `docshare/auth.py` (tokens and the active organisation), `docshare/routes/` (`files.py`, `folders.py`,\r\n`thumbs.py`, `export.py`, `share.py`, `admin.py`), `docshare/db.py` (schema and helpers), `docshare/seed.py`\r\n(development data).\r\n"]
[5.21611, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@0275029c-4ae8-4559-97b7-b32bc7ab9898:/app# "]
