[10.498345, "o", "| share | `POST /api/files/<id>/shares`, `DELETE /api/shares/<token>` | yes | yes | no |\r\n    36\t| delete | `DELETE /api/files/<id>` | no | yes | no |\r\n    37\t| support console | `GET /api/admin/orgs` | no | no | yes |\r\n    38\t| who am I | `GET /api/me` | yes | yes | yes |\r\n    39\t\r\n    40\t- For member and org_admin, \"yes\" means: on files and folders of the active organisation only (section 2).\r\n    41\t- For support, \"any organisation\" means: any file of any organisation, whatever the active organisation is.\r\n    42\t- A list shows exactly the folders or files of the active organisation, and nothing of any other organisation.\r\n    43\t\r\n    44\t## 4. Export\r\n    45\t`POST /api/export` returns several files in one response. It is allowed only if the caller may `read` every requested\r\n    46\tid under the rules above. If even one id is not readable (a file of another organisation, a deleted file, an unknown\r\n    47\tid), the whole request is refused and the response holds no file at all.\r\n"]
