[27.314058, "o", "printf '%s\\n' '===== API 1-90 ====='; sed -n '1,90p' docs/API.md; printf '%s\\n' '===== API 91-180 ====='; sed -n '91,180p' docs/API.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[27.314105, "o", "===== API 1-90 =====\r\n"]
[27.316394, "o", "# docshare API\r\n\r\ndocshare serves the documents that the ingest worker stores in its SQLite database (uploads go through the ingest\r\n"]
[27.316469, "o", "worker, not this API). Who may call what is in `PERMISSIONS.md`.\r\n\r\n## Running it\r\n```\r\npython -m docshare.serve --db <path to the SQLite file> --port <port>\r\n```\r\n"]
[27.316538, "o", "The service listens on 127.0.0.1, uses the database file given by `--db` (it must exist; the service never creates\r\none) and keeps all its state there. `python -m docshare.seed --out <path>` builds a fresh development database.\r\n\r\n## Conventions\r\n- Logged-in requests send `Authorization: Bearer <token>`; `X-Org-Id: <organisation id>` chooses the active\r\n  organisation (`PERMISSIONS.md` section 2).\r\n- Request and response bodies are JSON unless stated. Errors are JSON `{\"error\": \"<code>\"}`.\r\n- Ids are UUID strings. Times are ISO 8601 strings in UTC, for example `2026-09-14T10:22:05Z`.\r\n\r\n## Objects\r\n**File**: `id`, `org_id`, `folder_id`, `name`, `mime_type`, `size` (bytes, integer), `uploaded_by` (user id),\r\n`created_at`.\r\n\r\n**Folder**: `id`, `org_id`, `name`.\r\n\r\n## Endpoints\r\n"]
[27.316572, "o", "| Method and path | Success | Body of a successful response |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| `GET /api/health` | 200 | `{\"ok\": true}`; no login |\r\n| `GET /api/me` | 200 | `{\"user\": {\"id\", \"email\", \"name\", \"is_support\"}, \"active_org_id\", \"role\", \"memberships\": [{\"org_id\", \"role\"}]}`; `active_org_id` is `null` and `role` is `\"support\"` for support without `X-Org-Id` |\r\n| `GET /api/files` | 200 | `{\"files\": [File, ...]}`: the files of the active organisation, sorted by name |\r\n| `GET /api/folders` | 200 | `{\"folders\": [Folder, ...]}`: the folders of the active organisation, sorted by name |\r\n| `GET /api/folders/<folder_id>/files` | 200 | `{\"folder\": Folder, \"files\": [File, ...]}`, files sorted by name |\r\n| `GET /api/files/<file_id>` | 200 | File |\r\n| `GET /api/files/<file_id>/download` | 200 | the file's bytes, with its `mime_type` as Content-Type and `Content-Disposition: attachment; filename=\"<name>\"` |\r\n| `GET /api/files/<file_id>/thumb` | 200 | an `image/svg+xml` preview: the file name and the first lines of a text file "]
[27.316616, "o", "|\r\n| `PATCH /api/files/<file_id>` with `{\"name\": \"<new name>\"}` | 200 | the updated File; the name must be 1 to 200 characters without `/`, else `400` |\r\n| `DELETE /api/files/<file_id>` | 204 | empty; the file and its share links are removed |\r\n| `POST /api/files/<file_id>/shares` | 201 | `{\"token\", \"url\", \"file_id\", \"created_at\"}`; `url` is `/s/<token>` |\r\n| `DELETE /api/shares/<token>` | 204 | empty; the link stops working |\r\n| `GET /s/<token>` | 200 | the file's bytes, like download; no login |\r\n| `POST /api/export` with `{\"file_ids\": [<id>, ...]}` (1 to 50 ids) | 200 | `{\"files\": [{\"id\", \"name\", \"mime_type\", \"size\", \"content_b64\"}, ...]}` in request order; `content_b64` is the file's bytes in standard base64 |\r\n| `GET /api/admin/orgs` | 200 | `{\"orgs\": [{\"id\", \"name\", \"file_count\"}, ...]}` sorted by name |\r\n\r\nMalformed bodies (for example a missing `name`, or `file_ids` that is not a list of 1 to 50 strings) get `400`.\r\n\r\n## Database\r\nThe schema is in `docshare/db.py` (`SCHEMA`). Tables: `orgs`, `users`, "]
[27.316651, "o", "`memberships`, `folders`, `files` (contents\r\nare stored in `files.content`), `shares` (`revoked_at` is set when a link is revoked).\r\n"]
[27.316759, "o", "===== API 91-180 =====\r\n"]
[27.319695, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@0275029c-4ae8-4559-97b7-b32bc7ab9898:/app# "]
[33.905042, "i", "nl -ba docshare/db.py\n"]
[33.905191, "o", "nl -ba docshare/db.py\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[33.906278, "o", "     1\t\"\"\"SQLite access. One connection per request (see app.py); rows come back as sqlite3.Row.\"\"\"\r\n     2\timport sqlite3\r\n     3\t\r\n     4\tfrom flask import g\r\n     5\t\r\n"]
[33.906333, "o", "     6\tSCHEMA = \"\"\"\r\n     7\tCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS orgs (\r\n     8\t    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\r\n     9\t    name TEXT NOT NULL\r\n    10\t);\r\n    11\tCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS users (\r\n"]
[33.906372, "o", "    12\t    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\r\n    13\t    email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,\r\n    14\t    name TEXT NOT NULL,\r\n    15\t    token TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,\r\n    16\t    home_org_id TEXT REFERENCES orgs(id),\r\n    17\t    is_support INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0\r\n    18\t);\r\n    19\tCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS memberships (\r\n    20\t    user_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id),\r\n    21\t    org_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES orgs(id),\r\n    22\t    role TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (role IN ('member', 'org_admin')),\r\n    23\t    PRIMARY KEY (user_id, org_id)\r\n    24\t);\r\n    25\tCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS folders (\r\n    26\t    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\r\n    27\t    org_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES orgs(id),\r\n    28\t    name TEXT NOT NULL\r\n    29\t);\r\n"]
[33.906404, "o", "    30\tCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS files (\r\n    31\t    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\r\n    32\t    org_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES orgs(id),\r\n    33\t    folder_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES folders(id),\r\n    34\t    name TEXT NOT NULL,\r\n    35\t    mime_type TEXT NOT NULL,\r\n    36\t    size INTEGER NOT NULL,\r\n    37\t    content BLOB NOT NULL,\r\n    38\t    uploaded_by TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id),\r\n    39\t    created_at TEXT NOT NULL\r\n    40\t);\r\n"]
[33.906462, "o", "    41\tCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS shares (\r\n    42\t    token TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\r\n    43\t    file_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES files(id),\r\n    44\t    created_by TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id),\r\n    45\t    created_at TEXT NOT NULL,\r\n    46\t    revoked_at TEXT\r\n    47\t);\r\n    48\tCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS files_org ON files(org_id, name);\r\n    49\tCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS files_folder ON files(folder_id, name);\r\n    50\tCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS shares_file ON shares(file_id);\r\n    51\t\"\"\"\r\n    52\t\r\n    53\t"]
[33.90652, "o", "FILE_COLUMNS = \"id, org_id, folder_id, name, mime_type, size, uploaded_by, created_at\"\r\n    54\t\r\n    55\t\r\n    56\tdef connect(path):\r\n    57\t    conn = sqlite3.connect(path, timeout=10)\r\n    58\t    conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\r\n    59\t    conn.execute(\"PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON\")\r\n    60\t    conn.execute(\"PRAGMA busy_timeout = 10000\")\r\n    61\t    return conn\r\n    62\t\r\n    63\t\r\n    64\tdef get_db():\r\n    65\t    if \"db\" not in g:\r\n    66\t        from flask import current_app\r\n    67\t        g.db = connect(current_app.config[\"DB_PATH\"])\r\n    68\t    return g.db\r\n    69\t\r\n    70\t\r\n"]
[33.906554, "o", "    71\tdef close_db(_exc=None):\r\n    72\t    conn = g.pop(\"db\", None)\r\n    73\t    if conn is not None:\r\n    74\t        conn.close()\r\n    75\t\r\n    76\t\r\n    77\tdef query_one(sql, params=()):\r\n    78\t    return get_db().execute(sql, params).fetchone()\r\n    79\t\r\n    80\t\r\n    81\tdef query_all(sql, params=()):\r\n    82\t    return get_db().execute(sql, params).fetchall()\r\n    83\t\r\n    84\t\r\n    85\tdef execute(sql, params=()):\r\n"]
[33.9066, "o", "    86\t    conn = get_db()\r\n    87\t    cur = conn.execute(sql, params)\r\n    88\t    conn.commit()\r\n    89\t    return cur.rowcount\r\n    90\t\r\n    91\t\r\n    92\tdef file_json(row):\r\n    93\t    return {\"id\": row[\"id\"], \"org_id\": row[\"org_id\"], \"folder_id\": row[\"folder_id\"], \"name\": row[\"name\"],\r\n    94\t            \"mime_type\": row[\"mime_type\"], \"size\": row[\"size\"], \"uploaded_by\": row[\"uploaded_by\"],\r\n    95\t            \"created_at\": row[\"created_at\"]}\r\n    96\t\r\n    97\t\r\n    98\tdef folder_json(row):\r\n    99\t    return {\"id\": row[\"id\"], \"org_id\": row[\"org_id\"], \"name\": row[\"name\"]}\r\n"]
